# review-skills config -- KEY=VALUE, one per line. Keep this file mode 600: it holds API keys.
# The environment beats this file. Only keys named in it are read: the ones below, plus any other
# PR_REVIEW_* / PEER_REVIEW_* / OLLAMA_* / AGY_DO_* / AUTOFIX_MODEL|EFFORT|BUDGET key; anything else
# is ignored. Defaults are shown; each skill's SKILL.md says what a key does in full.
# `review-skills doctor` shows what is set (never the values) and which models will run.

# --- Backends. Any one is enough; each one added widens the choice of models. ---------------
# claude: sign in with `claude auth login` (subscription). To bill an API key instead:
# ANTHROPIC_USE_API_KEY=1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Run claude reviews under a separate subscription login (ignored with ANTHROPIC_USE_API_KEY=1).
# Create it once with: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<dir> claude auth login
# REVIEW_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-review
# agy (Gemini): sign in with agy itself; it takes no key.
# ollama.com: hosted open models (glm, kimi, ...). The diff leaves your machine when used.
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# --- Models. auto (default) picks the best reachable from lib/models.tsv; manual takes its first rows.
# REVIEW_SKILLS_MODELS=auto
# Pins, as transport:model[@effort], space-separated for several finders:
# PR_REVIEW_FINDERS=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5@medium
# PR_REVIEW_REFUTER=agy:gemini-3.8-flash-high
# PR_REVIEW_INTENSE_FINDERS=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5@medium agy:gemini-3.8-flash-high
# PR_REVIEW_INTENSE_REFUTER=ollama:glm-5.3-flash
# An unpinned refuter is a chain tried within one run; set the order yourself (this wins):
# PR_REVIEW_REFUTER_CHAIN=agy:gemini-3.8-flash-high ollama:glm-5.3-flash anthropic:claude-opus-5-5
# Per-call ceilings: stage 1 (one finder slice) and one refuter call. PR_REVIEW_AGY_TIMEOUT is
# the deprecated name of the refuter one.
# PR_REVIEW_S1_TIMEOUT=25m
# PR_REVIEW_REFUTE_TIMEOUT=8m
# peer-review: regular (default) or intense (same as --intense)
# PEER_REVIEW_ENGINE=regular
# Effort for the fix-PR implementer (never above medium)
# AUTOFIX_EFFORT=medium

# --- Where reviews are kept: <store>/<author>/<repo>/<N>/. Intense: <store>/_intense/... -----
# PR_REVIEW_DIR=~/.reviews

# --- Fix PRs. PR authors (GitHub logins, space- or comma-separated) whose confirmed findings
# get a companion fix PR instead of a report. Empty: never. -------------------------------
# PR_REVIEW_FIX_AUTHORS=
# (PEER_REVIEW_FIX_AUTHORS is an alias.)

# --- Which diff files are tests (reviewed in their own pass) and which earn a cross-cutting
# pass. Defaults suit Dart; extended regexes matched against the file path. -----------------
# PR_REVIEW_TEST_RE=(^|/)tests?/|_test\.dart$
# PR_REVIEW_CROSS_RE=(pubspec\.yaml|/lib/[^/]+\.dart)$

# --- Learning. A Markdown file (optional front-matter `description:`) pinned once as a rule the
# request-changes body writer follows. Default: posting-style.md beside this file, if present.
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN_SEED=~/.config/review-skills/posting-style.md
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN=off
# Where the learning engine keeps its state. Default: $PR_REVIEW_STATE/learn (~/.local/state/pr-review/learn).
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN_DIR=
# The model and effort for its LLM calls, and the claude binary it runs.
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN_EFFORT=medium
# PR_REVIEW_LEARN_CLAUDE=claude

# --- Tuning: stage 1 (finders) --------------------------------------------------------------
# PR_REVIEW_S1_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# PR_REVIEW_S1_EFFORT=medium
# PR_REVIEW_SONNET_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# PR_REVIEW_TRANSPORT=anthropic   (ollama sends stage 1 through ollama.com)
# PR_REVIEW_BUDGET_USD=8.00
# PR_REVIEW_STAGE1_JOBS=5
# PR_REVIEW_CHUNK_BYTES=80000
# PR_REVIEW_BRIEF_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# PR_REVIEW_BRIEF_EFFORT=medium
# PR_REVIEW_BRIEF_BUDGET_USD=1.00

# --- Tuning: stage 2 (refuters) --------------------------------------------------------------
# PR_REVIEW_JOBS=8
# PR_REVIEW_BURDEN=strict
# PR_REVIEW_REFUTER_FALLBACK=claude-opus-4-6-thinking
# PR_REVIEW_INTENSE_DIR=~/.reviews/_intense

# --- Fix PRs (autofix) -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTOFIX_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# AUTOFIX_BUDGET=8.00
# These autofix keys are read from the environment only: config.env drops them (see load_config in
# lib/common.sh), so export them in the shell that runs autofix.sh or peer-review.sh.
#   AUTOFIX_IMPLEMENTERS=claude ollama
#   AUTOFIX_OLLAMA_MODEL=glm-5.3
#   AUTOFIX_LINT_LEVEL=warning
#   AUTOFIX_DEFER_FALLBACK=18000   seconds a deferred run waits when no reset time is known (default: one five-hour window)
#   AUTOFIX_STANDARDS="$HOME/work/SE.md $HOME/work/SECURITY.md"   standards files inlined into the implementer's prompt (default shown; a missing one is skipped)
